# W44-228c1 SHIP-cell validation — meta

**Status**: FAIL → KEEP-OPT-IN-ONLY (W44-228b state stands as final)

**Date**: 2026-05-23
**Host**: lilith-wsl2 (water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM)
**Commit**: encoded against tree at jj parent `b8a60ca0` (W44-228b shipped opt-in API)
**Reproducer**: `cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --features '__expert tuning-override parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' --example w44_228c1_ship_cell_validation -- --output benchmarks/w44_228c1_ship_cell_validation_2026-05-23.tsv`
**TSV**: `benchmarks/w44_228c1_ship_cell_validation_2026-05-23.tsv` (12 rows, 1 cell per row)

## Goal

Resolve `docs/HYPOTHESIS_LEDGER.md` belief #18 (W44-228a per-stratum
optimum claim, status PROVEN at the global-coverage scale) against the
W44-105 SHIP-cell caveat surfaced in the W44-228a memo: every per-stratum
optimum on screen-class content sets
`screenshot_quant_aggressiveness = 0`, which effectively DISABLES the
W44-105 buttloop screen-seed lift. W44-105 was a measured SHIP that fixed
SSIM2 wins on terminal / imac_g3 / codec_wiki text at d=4-6, e8+.

Two competing explanations from the W44-228a memo / phase B closeout
memo:

- (a) **Corpus-composition artifact**: the W44-219 corpus that informed
  the W44-228a per-stratum optima under-represents the W44-105 SHIP
  cells, so the "reroute via the other 4 knobs" looks equivalent on the
  W44-219 corpus but is not equivalent on the W44-105 SHIP cells
  themselves.
- (b) **Genuine improvement**: the 4-knob reroute IS an equivalent or
  better operating point on screen-class generally, including the
  W44-105 SHIP cells.

W44-228c1 measures DIRECTLY on the SHIP cells to falsify (a) or (b).

## Method

12 W44-105 SHIP cells (3 images × 4 (effort, distance)):
- terminal.png, imac_g3.png, codec_wiki.png from `~/work/codec-corpus/gb82-sc/`
- (effort, distance) ∈ {(8, 4.0), (8, 5.0), (9, 4.0), (9, 5.0)}

Per cell, encode twice with `EncoderStrategy::Zenjxl`, 8 threads, 8 GiB
memory budget:
- **A (default)**: `LossyConfig::with_knobs(Tier2Knobs::default())`
- **B (auto)**: `LossyConfig::with_knobs(Tier2Knobs::auto_for_distance(ImageContentClass::Screenshot, distance))`

For ScreenVeryHigh stratum (`d ≥ 3.5`, which covers all 12 cells) the
auto knob tuple is `(k1=0.0, k2=0.0, k3=0.5, k4=1.5, k5=0.0)`. Per
[`expand_to_runtime_tuning`](../jxl-encoder/src/tuning.rs) this expands
to roughly:
- `p1_smart_zenjxl_photo_mask_p25_min ≈ 192.86` (loosest screen
  admission via smoothness_bias=0)
- `p2_screenshot_median_threshold ≈ 108.15` (loosest, same axis)
- `p3_buttloop_default_screenshot_qf_seed_scale ≈ 0.0` (W44-105 lift
  DISABLED via screenshot_quant_aggressiveness=0)
- `p4_buttloop_qf_seed_scale_min_distance = 1.5` (gate fires at all
  d ≥ 1.5, but with p3 ≈ 0 the gate is moot)
- `p5_adaptive_quant_screenshot_qf_seed_scale_e5_e6 ≈ 1.0` (half of
  default 2.0)
- `p6_adaptive_quant_screenshot_qf_seed_scale_e7 ≈ 1.5` (half of
  default 3.0 via screen_quant_lift=0.5; aggressiveness=0 zeros out
  the other contributor)

3 trials per (cell, mode) — best-of-N reported for `encode_ms`; bytes
and metrics are deterministic so first trial wins.

**Critical sequencing**: ALL mode-A encodes ran first (no override
installed), THEN ALL mode-B encodes (single `runtime::install` for the
single ScreenVeryHigh knob tuple that covers all 12 cells). Interleaving
within the same process would silently corrupt mode-A measurements after
the first mode-B encode because `runtime::install` uses a `OnceLock` —
every consumer reads the installed override regardless of
`cfg.tier2_knobs`. The v1 bench attempt produced byte-identical A/B on
cells 2-12 because of this — falsified the very first encoded row of v2.

## Result

| Gate | Spec | Observed | Pass? |
|---|---|---|---|
| (1) Mean Δssim2 | ≥ -0.1 | **-5.7137** | **FAIL** |
| (2) Mean Δbytes_pct | ≤ +1.5% | **-30.2616%** | PASS |
| (3) Worst Δssim2 | ≥ -0.5 | **-8.5948** on codec_wiki e8 d=5.0 | **FAIL** |
| (4) Worst Δbytes_pct | ≤ +5.0% | **-23.8273%** on terminal e9 d=4.0 | PASS |

**OVERALL: FAIL** (2/4 gates fail catastrophically).

### Per-cell delta table

| image | effort | distance | Δbytes_pct | Δssim2 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| terminal.png | e8 | 4.0 | -33.40 % | -4.93 |
| terminal.png | e8 | 5.0 | -34.64 % | -4.60 |
| terminal.png | e9 | 4.0 | -23.83 % | -4.14 |
| terminal.png | e9 | 5.0 | -25.12 % | -3.72 |
| imac_g3.png | e8 | 4.0 | -31.94 % | -6.87 |
| imac_g3.png | e8 | 5.0 | -34.11 % | **-8.11** |
| imac_g3.png | e9 | 4.0 | -24.62 % | -5.84 |
| imac_g3.png | e9 | 5.0 | -26.64 % | -6.59 |
| codec_wiki.png | e8 | 4.0 | -36.03 % | -5.46 |
| codec_wiki.png | e8 | 5.0 | -36.85 % | **-8.59** ← worst |
| codec_wiki.png | e9 | 4.0 | -27.63 % | -4.07 |
| codec_wiki.png | e9 | 5.0 | -28.33 % | -5.64 |

Every cell loses 3.7-8.6 SSIM2 points (default 0.1 budget exceeded by
**~50-90×**). Every cell saves 23-37 % bytes. This is the W44-228 surface
"reroute via 4 other knobs" doing its job at the Pareto level the
W44-219 corpus rewards, but the operating point is on the wrong side of
the W44-105 cells' Pareto curve — they want quality, not bytes, in the
text-heavy d=4-6 regime.

## Decision

**Hypothesis (a) PROVEN, hypothesis (b) RULED-OUT**. The W44-219 corpus
under-represents the W44-105 SHIP cells. The W44-228 surface looks
equivalent on the W44-219 corpus aggregate but is catastrophically worse
on these specific cells.

**Production state retained**: `Tier2Knobs::default()` remains the
default behaviour. `Tier2Knobs::auto_for_distance` remains OPT-IN
behind an explicit `LossyConfig::with_knobs(...)` call. Default-on flip
**is structurally BLOCKED** on screen-class content at d ≥ 3.5; it would
revert the W44-105 SHIP wins on the only cells that explicitly motivated
that fix.

**Recommendation**: SKIP W44-228c2 (the planned 20-anchor stratified
bootstrap re-measurement is moot — even if it tightened the per-stratum
optimum, it cannot escape the W44-105 mechanism mismatch that
`screenshot_quant_aggressiveness=0` causes on screen/very_high text
content). W44-228b API is the final state.

## Follow-on candidates (NOT in W44-228c1 scope)

1. **Per-cell zenanalyze sub-discriminator** for ScreenVeryHigh: detect
   text-heavy screenshots (high edge_density + low flat_color_block_ratio)
   AT ENCODE TIME and route them through `Tier2Knobs::default()` while
   text-light screenshots use the W44-228a auto knobs. Same pattern as
   W44-91 / W44-96 in-encoder discriminator. Cost: ~5-10 ms per image,
   covers the W44-105 mechanism boundary directly. EV: re-opens W44-228c
   default-flip path with the W44-105 cells protected.

2. **Re-derive the W44-228a optima on a corpus that INCLUDES the W44-105
   SHIP cells**. Per the W44-228a memo §Surprising finding the
   "screenshot_quant_aggressiveness=0 on every screen optimum" pattern
   may be a corpus artifact specifically because the W44-219 corpus
   sampled the SUPPRESSIVE coupling cap. Adding the W44-105 cells to
   the optimization corpus might shift the optima to non-zero `k2`.
   Multi-week chunk (requires another sweep run + GBR fit + per-stratum
   grid search).

3. **Drop per-stratum dispatch in favor of per-cell zenanalyze MLP**
   (Phase B closeout memo Option 2 / Tier-3 MLP design). Bypasses the
   per-stratum aggregation entirely. Higher cost, more flexibility.

## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

- **DO NOT spawn W44-228c2 (20-anchor bootstrap)** — the FAIL is so deep
  (mean -5.71 SSIM2 vs -0.1 budget) that no anchor-set tightening can
  flip the decision.
- **DO NOT default-flip per-stratum dispatch for any screen stratum**
  without first solving the W44-105 mechanism mismatch (e.g. via
  follow-on #1 above).
- **DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any byte / SSIM2 delta** (per W44-66
  user correction). The bytes / SSIM2 differ because the auto knobs
  expand to a fundamentally different `RuntimeTuning` (`p3 ≈ 0` vs
  default `p3 = 4.0`), which routes the encoder through a different
  quant-field generation path on screenshot-class content.
- **DO NOT modify `EncoderStrategy::Libjxl` hashes** (this chunk
  preserved them — the runtime override only affects Zenjxl).
- **DO NOT re-bisect ScreenVeryHigh knob values without a per-cell
  discriminator** — the W44-219 corpus optimum is the wrong Pareto point
  for these cells, full stop. Bisection within the same Pareto region
  cannot fix that.

